  "summary": {
    "en": {
      "caveats": "The proposed framework is conceptual and its practical utility in real-world planning workflows has not yet been empirically tested.",
      "what": "This study presents the Detect-Diagnose-Predict-Design (D2PD) framework, a conceptual workflow designed to integrate computer vision analytics directly into urban planning. The framework was developed through a systematic literature review of 27 selected papers from an initial pool of 500, followed by a reflexive thematic analysis.",
      "why": "It bridges the gap between real-time crowd monitoring and physical urban intervention, transforming computer vision from a passive surveillance tool on operational dashboards into an active, evidence-based generator of design guidelines."
    }
